hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19652","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us from Ashath ibn Jabir al-Huddani from Makhul from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: An old man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leaning upon a staff of his, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have treacheries and immoralities, will I be forgiven. He said: Do you not testify there is no god but Allah. He said: Yes, and I testify you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Your treacheries and immoralities have been forgiven for you."
"19653","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman, and he is al-Rahabi, narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to us from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Ukaz, and said: Who has followed you in this matter. He said: A freeman and a slave, and with him were Abu Bakr and Bilal, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both. He said to me: Return until Allah Mighty and Majestic gives mastery to His Messenger. I came to him afterwards and said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you, something you know and I do not know, it does not harm you and Allah Mighty and Majestic will benefit me with it: Is there an hour better than an hour, and is there an hour to be feared in. He said: You have asked me about something no one before you asked me about. Allah Mighty and Majestic descends in the depth of the night and forgives except what is of association and transgression. Prayer is witnessed and attended, so pray until the sun rises. When it rises, refrain from prayer, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, and it is the prayer of the disbelievers, until it rises high. When the sun stands high, then pray, for prayer is attended and witnessed, until the day stands level. When the day stands level, refrain from prayer, for it is an hour in which Hell is stoked, until the shade declines. When the shade declines, then pray, for prayer is attended and witnessed, until the sun goes down toward setting. When it goes down, refrain from prayer until the sun sets, for it sets upon the two horns of Satan, and it is the prayer of the disbelievers."
"19654","Hushaym narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who followed you in this your matter. He said: A freeman and a slave, meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both. And Amr used to say after that: I saw myself, and I was indeed the fourth of Islam."
"19655","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Dinar, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Dhakwan from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who followed you in this matter. He said: A freeman and a slave. I said: What is Islam. He said: Good speech and feeding food. I said: What is faith. He said: Patience and liberality. He said: I said: Which Islam is best. He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: I said: Which faith is best. He said: Good character. He said: I said: Which prayer is best. He said: Length of standing. He said: I said: Which emigration is best. He said: That you abandon what your Lord Mighty and Majestic dislikes. He said: I said: Then which struggle is best. He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and his blood shed. He said: I said: Which hours are best. He said: The depth of the last night, then prayer is prescribed and witnessed until dawn rises. When dawn rises, there is no prayer except the two units until you pray Fajr. When you pray the dawn prayer, refrain from prayer until the sun rises. When the sun rises, it rises in the two horns of Satan, and the disbelievers pray to it, so refrain from prayer until it rises high. When it rises high, prayer is prescribed and witnessed until the shadow stands like a spear. When it is so, refrain from prayer until it declines. When it declines, prayer is prescribed and witnessed until the sun sets. When at its setting, refrain from prayer, for it sets or disappears in the two horns of Satan, and the disbelievers pray to it."
"19656","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu al-Fayd from Sulaym ibn Amir, he said: There was a covenant between Muawiyah and a people of the Romans, so Muawiyah set out. He said: He began to march in their land until they break it and he raids them, when a man called out from the side of the people: Fulfilment, no treachery. Then it was Amr ibn Abasah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever has a covenant between him and a people, let him not tighten a knot nor loosen it until its term passes or he casts it to them on equal terms."
"19657","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Luqman narrated to us from Abu Umamah from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: I said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no omission nor error. He said: I heard him saying: Whoever has three children born to him in Islam and they die before reaching the age of responsibility, Allah Mighty and Majestic will admit him into Paradise by His mercy to them."
"19658","And whoever grows a grey hair in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"19659","And whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic and it reaches the enemy, whether it hits or misses, it will be for him like freeing a slave."
"19660","And whoever frees a believing slave, Allah will free with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."
"19661","And whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, then Paradise has eight gates, Allah Mighty and Majestic will admit him through whichever of its gates of Paradise He wills."
"19662","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Shahr narrated to me, Abu Zabyah narrated to me, he said: Shurahbil ibn al-Simt called Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami and said: O Ibn Abasah, will you narrate to me a hadith you yourself heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in which there is no addition nor lie, and do not narrate to me from another who heard it from him other than you. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Mighty and Majestic says: My love has become due for those who love one another for My sake, and My love has become due for those who stand in ranks for My sake, and My love has become due for those who visit one another for My sake, and My love has become due for those who give to one another for My sake, and My love has become due for those who aid one another for My sake."
"19663","And Amr ibn Abasah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever man shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic and it reaches, missing or hitting, then for him of reward is like a slave he frees from the children of Ismail."
"19664","And whatever man grows a grey hair in the path of Allah, it is a light for him."
"19665","And whatever Muslim man frees a Muslim man, then every limb of the freed is with a limb of the freer a ransom for him from the Fire. And whatever Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, then every limb of the freed woman is with a limb of the freer woman a ransom for her from the Fire."
"19666","And whatever Muslim man sends forth for Allah Mighty and Majestic from his loins three who have not reached the age of responsibility, or a woman, then they are for him a veil from the Fire."
"19667","And whatever man stands for ablution intending prayer and completes the ablution to its places, he is safe from every sin or fault of his. If he stands for prayer, Allah Mighty and Majestic raises him a degree by it, and if he sits he sits safe. Shurahbil ibn al-Simt said: Did you hear this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Ibn Abasah. He said: Yes, by the One there is no god but Him, if I had not heard this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once or twice or three or four or five or six or seven times— and he stopped at seven— I would not have sworn, meaning I would not care not to narrate it to anyone of the people, but by Allah I do not know the number of what I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19668","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sad narrated to us from Khalid ibn Madan from Kathir ibn Murrah from Amr ibn Abasah, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds for Allah a mosque in which Allah Mighty and Majestic is remembered, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"19669","And whoever frees a Muslim soul, it will be his ransom from Hell."
"19670","And whoever grows a grey hair in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"19671","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Hariz narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to us the hadith of Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, when he said to Amr ibn Abasah: Narrate to us a hadith in which there is no addition nor deficiency. Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it will be his redemption from the Fire, limb for limb."
"19672","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd Abu Daws al-Yahsabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh al-Thumali narrated to us from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst two tribes among the Arabs are Najran and Banu Taghlib."
"19673","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Muslim narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Mawhab al-Amluki from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Sukun and al-Sakasik, and over Khawlan the High, and over al-Amluk, the Amluk of Radman."
"19674","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah from Humayd ibn Uqbah from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt from Amr ibn Abasah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fights in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic for the time of milking a camel, Allah will forbid his face from the Fire."
"19675","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, Shurayh ibn Ubayd narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aidh al-Azdi from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day displaying horses, and with him was Uyaynah ibn Hisn ibn Badr al-Fazari. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I am more skilled with horses than you. Uyaynah said: And I am more skilled with men than you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: And how is that. He said: The best of men are men carrying their swords upon their shoulders, placing their spears upon the looms of their horses, wearing striped cloaks, from the people of Najd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have lied, rather the best of men are the men of Yemen. Faith is Yemeni, toward Lakhm and Judham and Amilah. The eaten of Himyar is better than its eater. Hadramawt is better than Banu al-Harith. One tribe is better than a tribe, and one tribe is worse than a tribe. By Allah, I do not care if the two al-Hariths both perish. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamda and Mikhwasa and Mishrakha and Abdah, and their sister al-Amarradah. Then he said: My Lord Mighty and Majestic commanded me to curse Quraysh twice, so I cursed them. And He commanded me to pray over them, so I prayed over them twice. Then he said: Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, other than Qays and Jadah and Usayyah. Then he said: Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah and their allies of Juhaynah are better than Banu Asad and Tamim and Ghatafan and Hawazin, with Allah Mighty and Majestic on the Day of Resurrection. Then he said: The worst two tribes among the Arabs are Najran and Banu Taghlib. And the most numerous tribes in Paradise are Madhhij and Makul. He said: Abu al-Mughirah said: Safwan said: Himyar, Himyar is better than its eater. He said: Those who passed are better than those who remain."
"19676","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Habib ibn Ubayd from Amr ibn Abasah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Night prayer is two by two, and the depth of the last night is most responsive in supplication. I said: Most obligatory. He said: No, rather most responsive, meaning by that answering."
"19677","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Atiyyah ibn Qays from Amr ibn Abasah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"19678","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us from Atiyyah from Amr ibn Abasah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two, and the depth of the last night is most conducive to supplication. He said: I said: Most obligatory. He said: No, but most conducive, meaning by that answering."
"19679","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us from a man from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was displaying horses, and with him was Uyaynah ibn Hisn ibn Hudhayfah ibn Badr al-Fazari, he said to Uyaynah: I am more discerning about horses than you. Uyaynah said: And I am more discerning about men than you. He said: Then how is that. He said: The best of men are those who place their swords upon their shoulders and lay their spears upon the looms of their horses, from the people of Najd. He said: You have lied, the best of men are the men of Yemen. Faith is Yemeni, and I am Yemeni. The most numerous tribes on the Day of Resurrection in Paradise are Madhhij. Hadramawt is better than Banu al-Harith. I do not care if the two tribes both perish. There is no chief nor king except to Allah Mighty and Majestic. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamda and Mishrakha and Mikhwasa and Abdah, and their sister al-Amarradah."
